{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1554393878,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MjkzNjI2Njk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3290","origin":"github"},"title":"wishlist: benchmark of core functionality in case of untracked files","message":"came up as a result of review in #3288 \n\nI guess we need a benchmark which would operate in some \"dirty\" repo somewhat heavy on files, subdirectories and possibly submodules which are not yet tracked. And there we would benchmark `save` performance on tracked, and not yet tracked path(s).   \n\nLocal filesystem caching though would be an obstacle and unfortunately we would not be able to `echo` to `/proc/sys/vm/drop_caches` to flush. But we already do a small `sudo` evil in `test_ro_operations` (and skip if not possible), so may be we would be doomed to introduce something like that to this benchmark - otherwise it would always provide \"hot\" performance.","files":null}]}